\n) -> Result<(), WhirError> {\n    let shape = commitment.shape;\n    if !shape.valid()\n        || shape.log_batch_size != config.initial_k()\n        || config.log_inv_rates().first() != Some(&shape.log_inv_rate)\n        || commitment.point.len() != shape.log_n\n    {\n        return Err(WhirError::CommitmentMismatch);\n    }\n    super::commit::verify_record_binding(v, commitment)?;\n    let beta = v.sample();\n    let target = v.mul_add(beta, commitment.value, target);\n    let combined_weight = AnchoredWeight {\n        caller: weight_at,\n        shape,\n        point: &commitment.point,\n        beta,\n    };\n    verify_protocol_with_basis(\n        v,\n        config,\n        shape.log_n,\n        shape.n_lanes,\n        target,\n        commitment.root,\n        combined_weight,\n    )\n}","attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Succinct verifier for the recursive prover, against a weight `b` over the `2^log_n` committed words."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" It takes no dense weight: `weight_at` evaluates b's multilinear extension once, at the final fold point indexed by witness coordinate."},{"DocComment":" Verify a public linear claim with the same immutable commitment record used"},{"DocComment":" at commitment time. `weight_at` evaluates the claimed weight on the full"},{"DocComment":" Boolean cube and must vanish outside the record's occupied lane prefix."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The caller binds the public claim before entry. This samples only the"},{"DocComment":" opening batch scalar and reuses the commitment's point and advertised value."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Errors"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Returns an incompatible commitment/configuration, malformed opening stream,"},{"DocComment":" failed authentication, or a terminal opening that violates either claim."}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":true,"started_from":true,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null,"diagn